{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"We can expand this expression using the \"perfect square\" pattern (where $P$ and $Q$ can be any monomial):\n\n$(P+Q)^2=P^2+2PQ+Q^2$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}(P+Q)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=(P+Q)(P+Q)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=P(P+Q)+Q(P+Q)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=P^2+P\\cdot Q+Q\\cdot P+Q^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=P^2+2PQ+Q^2\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show me why this is true.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Since we have a minus sign, let's rewrite the binomial as a sum where the second term is negative, then use the pattern.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\left(2a^6-6a^3\\right)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\left(2a^6+\\left(-6a^3\\right)\\right)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=(2a^6)^2+2(2a^6)(-6a^3)+(-6a^3)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4a^{12}-24a^9+36a^6\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Expand and combine like terms.**\n\n$(2a^6-6a^3)^2=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"buttonsVisible":"focused","considered":"correct","form":true,"functions":["f","g","h"],"key":0,"linterContext":{"contentType":"","highlightLint":false,"paths":[],"stack":[]},"simplify":false,"times":false,"value":"4a^{12}-24a^{9}+36a^{6}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
